## EU Publications Office — EUR-Lex / CELLAR

EU directive metadata and full-text content are sourced from **EUR-Lex / CELLAR**,
made available by the **Publications Office of the European Union**. Reuse is
permitted under **Commission Decision 2011/833/EU**, which requires that the
source be acknowledged and that the data not be distorted:

- Source: EUR-Lex / CELLAR (Publications Office of the European Union)
- Reuse decision: <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011D0833>

Metadata is retrieved through the Publications Office SPARQL endpoint
(`https://publications.europa.eu/webapi/rdf/sparql`); full text through the
CELLAR content-delivery service. The data has been parsed and restructured into
the `seed/` object/relationship format by this project.

## Stortinget — Norwegian Licence for Open Government Data (NLOD 2.0)

Forarbeid (preparatory works) full text is sourced from the **Stortinget data
